// A hexadecimal literal whose value needs more than 64 bits is a static error
// (spec/01-lexical.md, row `hex-width`).
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). An implementation
// that runs the program fails this probe.

print 0x10000000000000000;

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
// COVERS: literal hex-width
